format session-log-v1
stamp 20260815.001849
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host Ubuntu cloud pier — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES103 — Lotus's peak normalize, measure the loudest sample then scale the clip so it lands exactly on a chosen target
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES102 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think The silence family (ALES96–102) is whole — strip, split, top-and-tail, pad, collapse, smooth, and the smoothed trim that ties them together. That family answered where is the sound? The next Lindy crux is the question a keeper asks the instant the sound is found: how loud is it, and can every take be the same loudness? Peak normalization — the Normalize button every editor and DAW ships, one click on a whole clip — is the single most-reached-for level gesture, and it is the first Lotus rung to fuse the reader (ALES13's meter) and the writer (ALES2's gain) into one tool. No normalize.rye existed yet.
think Shape: normalize_peak(clip, target), target a magnitude in [1, sample_max]. Measure the peak through ALES13's measure; a silent clip (peak 0) is left exactly as it is — no peak to lift, and that guard also keeps the division below from ever dividing by zero; else scale the whole clip [0, clip.len) by target/peak through ALES2's saturating gain. Amplify (peak below target) and attenuate (peak above target) are the same call, one fraction, two directions. No new arithmetic — measure then gain — so it can never drift from the meter it reads or the gain it delegates to.
think The peak law is the crux's heart: after normalize the new peak equals target exactly. The peak sample at magnitude peak maps to divTrunc(±peak·target, peak) = ±target exactly; every quieter sample |x| < peak maps to divTrunc(|x|·target, peak), strictly inside ±target (equality would need |x| ≥ peak). So nothing overshoots and the new peak is the target on the nose — including the i16 minimum −32768 (magnitude 32768) at the meter's domain ceiling, which normalizes to 32767 landing −32767. Because the peak lands exactly on target ≤ sample_max, no sample ever actually saturates: the ceiling is respected, never reached.
think Errors: NormalizeError = meter.MeterError || timeline.EditError || error{BadTarget}. The forwarded MeterFull (a Clip is bounded well inside the meter's 2^26 window) and BadGain/BadRange (a measured non-zero denominator, a whole-clip span) are honestly unreachable here, named for parity. BadTarget refuses a zero target (not a normalize) or a target past sample_max (no positive sample can reach it), before any read or write.
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — the scale law on two known peaks (×2 amplify to exact [8000,-16000,4000], ×0.5 attenuate to exact [10000,-15000,5000]); the peak law re-measured over 5 clips × 5 targets = 25 cases each landing the target exactly; the silence law on an all-zero and an empty clip at three targets; the idempotence law; amplify-vs-attenuate direction; and the two BadTarget refusals leaving the clip untouched. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged at 11), the peak/RMS meter and the saturating gain reused whole rather than re-derived.
obs No custody gate reached — software only, local; a plain sample magnitude, not a decibel or a loudness model (peak normalization, the plainest reading); no funds, keys, network, device, or real speaker. It changes sample values only through ALES2's gain, fabricating none and never a length.
loom witness=ales_normalize_witness green=1 laws=4 peak_law_grid=25 module_bytes=9k
file lotus/normalize.rye ALES103 — normalize_peak() measures the peak through ALES13 then scales the whole clip by target/peak through ALES2's gain; silent-clip and BadTarget guards at the edge.
file tools/ales_normalize_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line.
file active-designing/20260815-001849_fill-ales103-lotus-peak-normalize.md the self-approved design read naming the scale, peak, silence, and idempotence laws.
file lotus/README.md front door — the ALES103 rung prepended to the roster, appended to the status line, and the stamp synced.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus crux stays in the level family: an RMS normalize (target the ALES13 RMS rather than the peak, the loudness-matched twin of this peak reading), a normalize-to-headroom that leaves a named margin below full scale, or a per-region normalize over an ALES23 selection; each its own self-approved round, no custody gate reached.
